top-sort [sumsales asc, ss_customer_sk asc] limit 100
└─ project (ss_customer_sk, sumsales) (rows≈1 cost≈9.3K)
   └─ aggregate keys=[t.ss_customer_sk] aggs=[sum_0=sum] (rows≈1 cost≈9.2K)
      └─ project (t.ss_customer_sk, t.act_sales) (rows≈1 cost≈9.2K)
         └─ join inner [store_returns.sr_item_sk = store_sales.ss_item_sk, store_returns.sr_ticket_number = store_sales.ss_ticket_number] emit-filter 1 from left (rows≈1 cost≈9.2K)
            ├─ join inner [reason.r_reason_sk = store_returns.sr_reason_sk] emit-filter 2 from left (rows≈1 cost≈4.7K)
            │  ├─ filter (== |reason.r_reason_desc| (cast "Did not like the warranty" <named StringView>)) (rows≈1 cost≈400)
            │  │  └─ source reason AS reason row-groups (== |reason.r_reason_desc| (cast "Did not like the warranty" <named StringView>)) (rows≈10 cost≈200)
            │  └─ source store_returns AS store_returns use-filter 2 keys=[store_returns.sr_reason_sk] (rows≈10 cost≈160)
            └─ source store_sales AS store_sales use-filter 1 keys=[store_sales.ss_item_sk, store_sales.ss_ticket_number] (rows≈10 cost≈240)
